# Key Takeaway Edit Slide lock (do not regress)

Anthony (2026-11-02): Edit on Module Summary still showed leftover short OST bullets that are not on the slide, while the four numbered takeaway cards could not be changed. Switching the editor from bullets to a numbered list also did nothing.

`npm test` must stay green (`src/lib/keyTakeawayOst.test.ts`).

## Invariants (code, not comments)

- **Edit Text shows the cards.** For `key-takeaways`, Edit Slide does **not** render the leftover OST RichTextEditor. [`isKeyTakeawaysType`](src/lib/keyTakeawayOst.ts) gates that in [`App.tsx`](src/App.tsx).
- **Numbered statements are the fields.** [`keyTakeawayEditItems`](src/lib/keyTakeawayOst.ts) reads `normalizeKeyTakeaways(...).data.objectives` (player source), not leftover `content`. [`applyKeyTakeawayEdits`](src/lib/keyTakeawayOst.ts) writes **objectives plus numbered content** so Save updates the slide the learner sees.
- **Layout stays numbered.** The player uses numbered badges. The editor shows numbered fields, not a bullet/numbered list toggle. Do not require Regenerate to change a takeaway sentence.
- **Add is available.** Authors can add takeaways up to `MAX_KEY_TAKEAWAYS` (8). Hydrate still generates 2–4. Do not hide Add just because four cards already exist.
- **One version everywhere.** [`keyTakeawayEditItems`](src/lib/keyTakeawayOst.ts) / [`takeawayCardStatement`](src/lib/keyTakeawayOst.ts) is the player card text. Review (`buildReviewScriptModel`) uses that list only — no leftover `content` intro and no duplicate per-objective sections. `npm test` must stay green (`src/lib/reviewAlignment.test.ts`).
- **Keep the player layout.** Do not put leftover short OST bullets back on the Module Summary canvas.

## How to change this

Change the helpers and add a failing test first. Do not “fix” Edit by putting the cards into on-screen text.
